]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={v}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing our two solutions, we see that the vector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ satisfies $(A-6I)^{2}v=0$ but does *not* satisfy $(A-6I)v=0.$  \n\nHence, $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ of $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397924 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397924 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397924 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397924 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397924 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397924 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397924 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397924 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186397927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397924 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2dca7bc2-b356-50e5-bfa8-29c4a44dbc8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397925 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397925 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397925 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d532b568-40fd-5c42-bd50-9c531a27d8f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397926 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397926 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397926 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7be7d0d9-fe40-5825-a710-69d11c7d3940" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397927 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397927 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397927 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0178b2e4-7a61-5504-922f-6c54eb1b2c87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397928 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{ali